{"title": "ALG AVS111C-Y stereo module", "parts": {"lead": "<p class=lead>GMSL2 stereo camera module from Shenzhen Aili-Light Technology (ALG Tech, 艾利光), with two global-shutter cameras 50 mm apart and a 6-axis IMU. Three recordings, each solved as stereo + IMU; this page shows the longest. The recordings match ALG&#x27;s AVS111C-Y; the exact model isn&#x27;t confirmed by the maker.</p><div class=chips><span class=chip>Stereo</span><span class=chip>Global shutter</span><span class=chip>200 Hz IMU</span><span class=chip>GMSL2</span></div>", "glance": "<p>GMSL2 stereo camera module from Shenzhen Aili-Light Technology (ALG Tech, 艾利光), with two global-shutter cameras 50 mm apart and a 6-axis IMU. Three recordings, each solved as stereo + IMU; this page shows the longest. The recordings match ALG&#x27;s AVS111C-Y; the exact model isn&#x27;t confirmed by the maker.</p><div class=band><div class=\"demo empty\"><b>No video on this page.</b> The values below come from the solved run.</div><div class=v data-v=\"0\"><div class=tiles><div><span>Reprojection median</span><b>0.11<small> px</small></b></div><div><span>cam0–cam1 baseline</span><b>49.9<small> mm</small></b></div><div><span>cam0 td</span><b>−16.32<small> ms</small></b></div><div><span>cam0 lever arm</span><b>46.6<small> mm</small></b></div></div></div></div><p class=sd-note>Reprojection is how far, in pixels, the detected corners lie from where the solve puts them. td is the camera–IMU time offset, and the lever arm is the camera–IMU position offset.</p><p class=sd-note>No independent reference, so these values show what MVIS solved, not how close they are to the truth.</p>", "process": "<p>The path of the rig around the board, as MVIS solved it. To explore it:</p><ul class=list><li>Press <b>Play</b> or drag the bar to follow the path.</li><li>Use the <b>view buttons</b> to change the view.</li><li>Pick a <b>camera card</b> to put that camera on the frustum, the pyramid that shows its view.</li></ul><p>Each card draw