ing; the exact model isn&#x27;t confirmed</td><td><span class=chip>Maker</span></td></tr><tr><td>Cameras</td><td>2 × 1280×800, 30 Hz with no dropped frames in these recordings</td><td><span class=chip>Measured</span></td></tr><tr><td>Shutter</td><td>Global on the AVS111C-Y sheet; a rolling-shutter solve of an earlier recording found no readout</td><td><span class=chip>Measured</span></td></tr><tr><td>Lens</td><td>1.67 mm, 120° horizontal on the AVS111C-Y sheet</td><td><span class=chip>Maker</span></td></tr><tr><td>IMU</td><td>6-axis, up to 6400 Hz on the sheet; 200 Hz in these recordings</td><td><span class=chip>Maker</span></td></tr><tr><td>Link and power</td><td>GMSL2, power over coax, 9 to 12 V</td><td><span class=chip>Maker</span></td></tr></tbody></table></div><p class=note>Maker's specs from <a href=\"https://www.aili-light.com/machine-vision-stereo-camera/AVS111C-X-machine-vision-stereo-camera.html\">ALG AVS111C-Y product page</a>, checked 2026-11-11.</p><p class=note>Company: <a href=\"https://www.aili-light.com/\">Shenzhen Aili-Light Technology (ALG Tech)</a>.</p>", "dataset": "<div class=two><div class=scroll><table><tbody><tr><td>Recordings</td><td>3 recordings of 112, 144 and 148 s. Shown: the 148 s one, cam0 4,433 frames, cam1 4,432, IMU 29,516 samples</td></tr><tr><td>Format</td><td>ROS2 bag with compressed images, converted to EuRoC layout</td></tr><tr><td>Board</td><td>ChArUco 14×9 squares, 40 mm squares, 30 mm markers</td></tr><tr><td>Licence</td><td>None</td></tr><tr><td>Hosted</td><td>Not hosted</td></tr></tbody></table></div><div><figure class=board><svg viewBox=\"-40.0 -40.0 640.0 440.0\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"ChArUco board 9 by 14 squares, to scale\"><rect x=\"-40.0\" y=\"-40.0\" width=\"640.0\" height=\"440.0\" fill=\"#fff\"/><path fill=\"#111\" d=\"M0.00 0.00h40.00v40.00h-40.00zM45.00 5.00h30.00v30.00h-30.00zM80.00 0.00h40.00v40.00h-40.00zM125.00 5.00h30.00v30.00h-30.00zM160.00 0.00h40.00v40.00h-40.00zM205.00 5.00h30.00v30.00h-30.00zM240.