284.5,123.8 301.0,116.8 317.5,109.7 333.9,102.6 350.4,95.3 366.9,88.0 383.3,80.5 399.8,72.8 416.3,64.8 432.7,56.3 449.2,47.2 465.7,37.1 482.1,25.7 498.6,12.6\"/><polyline class=\"c1\" points=\"54.0,220.0 70.5,213.2 86.9,206.4 103.4,199.6 119.9,192.8 136.3,185.9 152.8,179.1 169.3,172.2 185.7,165.4 202.2,158.5 218.7,151.6 235.1,144.7 251.6,137.7 268.1,130.7 284.5,123.7 301.0,116.6 317.5,109.6 333.9,102.5 350.4,95.5 366.9,88.5 383.3,81.7 399.8,75.0 416.3,68.8 432.7,63.1 449.2,58.3 465.7,54.5 482.1,52.4 498.6,52.5 515.1,55.4 531.5,62.2 548.0,73.9\"/></svg></div></div><p class=legend><i class=c0></i>cam0 <i class=c1></i>cam1 </p><p class=note>We read these from the calibrated lens fit at the image edges, through the principal point (where the optical axis meets the image). ~ marks an axis past where the corners reached, so the fit is extrapolated there. Past the fit means an edge lies beyond where the fit holds, so we give no value.</p>", "imu": "<div class=v data-v=\"0\"><p>Each bar shows a scale as its deviation from 1. IMU model: calyx. <code>t_ga</code>, the time offset between the gyroscope and accelerometer channels: +0.84 ± 0.83 ms.</p><div class=bars><div class=bar><span>Gyro scale x</span><i><u style=\"left:50.00%;width:3.29%\"></u></i><b>+0.53 %</b></div><div class=bar><span>Gyro scale y</span><i><u style=\"left:50.00%;width:1.60%\"></u></i><b>+0.26 %</b></div><div class=bar><span>Gyro scale z</span><i><u style=\"left:49.69%;width:0.31%\"></u></i><b>−0.05 %</b></div><div class=bar><span>Accel scale x</span><i><u style=\"left:50.00%;width:1.47%\"></u></i><b>+0.24 %</b></div><div class=bar><span>Accel scale y</span><i><u style=\"left:50.00%;width:1.06%\"></u></i><b>+0.17 %</b></div><div class=bar><span>Accel scale z</span><i><u style=\"left:50.00%;width:1.04%\"></u></i><b>+0.17 %</b></div><div class=bar><span></span><em><s>−8 %</s><s>0</s><s>+8 %</s></em><b></b></div></div></div>", "timing": "<p>The time offsets, to scale. td is the camera–IMU time offset, with t_imu = t_cam + td.</p><div class=v data-v=\"0\"><div class=chart><svg viewBox=\"0 0 560 136\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Time offsets in milliseconds, to scale\"><line class=\"g\" x1=70.0 x2=70.0 y1=4 y2=112 /><text x=70.0 y=128 text-anchor=middle>-20 ms</text><line class=\"g\" x1=177.5 x2=177.5 y1=4 y2=112 /><text x=177.5 y=128 text-anchor=middle>-10 ms</text><line class=\"g z\" x1=285.0 x2=285.0 y1=4 y2=112 /><text x=285.0 y=128 text-anchor=middle>+0 ms</text><line class=\"g\" x1=392.5 x2=392.5 y1=4 y2=112 /><text x=392.5 y=128 text-anchor=middle>+10 ms</text><line class=\"g\" x1=500.0 x2=500.0 y1=4 y2=112 /><text x=500.0 y=128 text-anchor=middle>+20 ms</text><text x=0 y=22>cam0 td</text><line class=stem x1=285.0 x2=109.5 y1=18 y2=18 /><circle class=dot cx=109.5 cy=18 r=5 /><text x=100.5 y=22 text-anchor=end>−16.32</text><text x=0 y=56>cam1 td</text><line class=stem x1=285.0 x2=109.0 y1=52 y2=52 /><circle class=dot cx=109.0 cy=52 r=5 /><text x=100.0 y=56 text-anchor=end>−16.37</text><text x=0 y=90>t_ga</text><line class=stem x1=285.0 x2=294.0 y1=86 y2=86 /><circle class=dot cx=294.0 cy=86 r=5 /><text x=303.0 y=90 text-anchor=start>+0.84</text></svg></div></div>", "results": "<p>Rotation is log(R) in rad, camera in the IMU frame.</p><div class=v data-v=\"0\"><div class=scroll><table class=num><thead><tr><th>Parameter</th><th>MVIS</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr class=grp><th colspan=2>cam0</th></tr><tr><td>fx px</td><td>599.32</td></tr><tr><td>fy px</td><td>599.42</td></tr><tr><td>cx px</td><td>624.50</td></tr><tr><td>cy px</td><td>399.97</td></tr><tr><td>k1</td><td>0.01191</td></tr><tr><td>k2</td><td>0.01856</td></tr><tr><td>k3</td><td>−0.02284</td></tr><tr><td>k4</td><td>0.01333</td></tr><tr><td>Lever x mm</td><td>+42.15</td></tr><tr><td>Lever y mm</td><td>+8.03</td></tr><tr><td>Lever z mm</td><td>−18.27</td></tr><tr><td>log(R) rad</td><td>[+0.0064, −3.1398, +0.0023]</td></tr><tr><td>td ms</td><td>−16.322</td></tr><tr><td>Reprojection px</td><td>0.142</td></tr><tr class=grp><th colspan=2>cam1</th></tr><tr><td>fx px</td><td>597.69</td></tr><tr><td>fy px</td><td>597.62</td></tr><tr><td>cx px</td><td>622.44</td></tr><tr><td>cy px</td><td>405.33</td></tr><tr><td>k1</td><td>0.01709</td></tr><tr><td>k2</td><td>0.00502</td></tr><tr><td>k3</td><td>0.00738</td></tr><tr><td>k4</td><td>−0.01263</td></tr><tr><td>Lever x mm</td><td>−7.76</td></tr><tr><td>Lever y mm</td><td>+8.10</td></tr><tr><td>Lever z mm</td><td>−18.73</td></tr><tr><td>log(R) rad</td><td>[−0.0246, +3.1360, −0.0012]</td></tr><tr><td>td ms</td><td>−16.371</td></tr><tr><td>Reprojection px</td><td>0.145</td></tr><tr class=grp><th colspan=2>IMU</th></tr><tr><td>t_ga ms</td><td>+0.84 ± 0.83</td></tr></tbody></table></div></div>", "limits": "<ul class=list><li>No independent reference, so these values show what MVIS solved, not how close they are to the truth.</li><li>We solved three recordings of the same unit separately. The lever arm agrees within 3 mm, the camera-to-IMU time offset within 0.2 ms, the focal lengths within 1.3 px and the IMU scales within 0.4 %. The IMU position also agrees with the maker&#x27;s drawing within 2 mm.</li><li>The board reaches about 54° off-axis. Past that, toward the image edges (61°) and corners (72°), the lens model is extrapolated: the three solves differ by up to 7 px at the edges and 35 px at the corners.</li><li>The motion is gentle (about 6 to 11°/s RMS), so the lever arm is the least certain value, with a solver σ of 2 to 4 mm.</li><li>The model is matched from resolution, baseline, field of view and shutter, not confirmed by the maker.</li></ul>", "run": "<ul class=list><li>Both cameras and the IMU, global shutter, default IMU noise, t_ga estimated, camera intrinsics free. The IMU stored accel 4× and gyro 2× too small; both were scaled before solving. Batch of 2026-11-11.</li></ul>", "header": "<div class=sd><div class=sd-grid><div class=sd-head><a class=sd-maker href=\"https://www.aili-light.com/\">Shenzhen Aili-Light Technology (ALG Tech) ↗︎</a><h1 id=\"_top\">ALG AVS111C-Y stereo module</h1><p class=sd-type>GMSL2 stereo camera module with a 6-axis IMU</p></div><figure class=sd-plate><div class=sd-frame><img src=\"/media/sensors/alg-avs111c/alg-avs111c.png\" alt=\"ALG AVS111C-Y stereo camera module\" width=\"800\" height=\"533\"></div><figcaption><a href=\"https://www.aili-light.com/machine-vision-stereo-camera/AVS111C-X-machine-vision-stereo-camera.html\">Photo: ALG Tech, AVS111C-Y product page. Closest published model; exact model not confirmed ↗︎</a></figcaption></figure><div class=sd-cta><div class=sd-buttons><a class=\"sd-btn primary\" href=\"https://www.aili-light.com/machine-vision-stereo-camera/AVS111C-X-machine-vision-stereo-camera.html\">Closest model: AVS111C-Y ↗︎</a><a class=sd-btn href=\"#specifications\">All specs (8) ↓</a></div></div><div class=sd-specs><dl class=sd-rows><div class=sd-row><dt>Cameras</dt><dd>2 × 1280×800<span class=sd-tag>Measured</span></dd></div><div class=sd-row><dt>Shutter</dt><dd>Global<a class=sd-tag href=\"https://www.aili-light.com/machine-vision-stereo-camera/AVS111C-X-machine-vision-stereo-camera.html\">Maker ↗︎</a></dd></div><div class=sd-row><dt>Field of view</dt><dd>Calibrated ~119° × 76°<span class=sd-tag>Measured</span></dd></div><div class=sd-row><dt>Baseline</dt><dd>49.9 mm<span class=sd-tag>Measured</span></dd></div><div class=sd-row><dt>IMU</dt><dd>6-axis, 200 Hz here<span class=sd-tag>Measured</span></dd></div><div class=sd-row><dt>Output</dt><dd>GMSL2, ROS2 bag<span class=sd-tag>Measured</span></dd></div></dl><p class=sd-foot>Values measured in the 148 s recording · Maker values from the AVS111C-Y product page, read 2026-11-06 · ~ marks a value read past where the board corners reached. Past the fit: the edge lies beyond where the lens fit holds, so we give no value.</p></div></div></div>", "specifications": "<div class=scroll><table class=spec-table><tbody><tr class=grp><th colspan=2>Published by the maker</th></tr><tr><td>Maker</td><td>Shenzhen Aili-Light Technology (ALG Tech)</td></tr><tr><td>Closest published model</td><td>AVS111C-Y: 1280×800, 50 mm baseline, 120° × 76°, global shutter. Matched from this recording; the exact model isn&#x27;t confirmed</td></tr><tr><td>Lens</td><td>1.67 mm, 120° horizontal on the AVS111C-Y sheet</td></tr><tr><td>IMU</td><td>6-axis, up to 6400 Hz on the sheet; 200 Hz in these recordings</td></tr><tr><td>Link and power</td><td>GMSL2, power over coax, 9 to 12 V</td></tr><tr class=grp><th colspan=2>Measured in these recordings</th></tr><tr><td>Cameras</td><td>2 × 1280×800, 30 Hz with no dropped frames in these recordings</td></tr><tr><td>Shutter</td><td>Global on the AVS111C-Y sheet; a rolling-shutter solve of an earlier recording found no readout</td></tr><tr><td>Calibrated field of view</td><td>cam0 ~119° × 76° · cam1 ~121° × 76°</td></tr></tbody></table></div><details class=fold id=\"sales-contact\"><summary>Sales contact <span>Provided by the maker</span></summary><div><div class=scroll><table class=spec-table><tbody><tr><td>Email</td><td><a href=\"mailto:sales@aili-light.com\">sales@aili-light.com</a></td></tr><tr><td>Phone</td><td><a href=\"tel:+8675527218150\">+86 755 2721 8150</a></td></tr></tbody></table></div></div></details>", "rig": "<p>The solved rig in 3D, to scale. Tap a sensor to see its values. In full screen you can rotate and zoom. Grid squares are 20 mm.</p><div class=map><div class=stage><canvas id=rig tabindex=0 aria-label=\"3D map of the cameras and IMU\"></canvas><div class=tools><button data-view=iso type=button>3D</button><button data-view=front type=button>Front</button><button data-view=top type=button>Top</button><button data-view=side type=button>Side</button><button data-z=1 type=button aria-label=\"Zoom in\">+</button><button data-z=-1 type=button aria-label=\"Zoom out\">−</button></div></div><div class=panel><div class=picks id=picks></div><div id=info></div></div></div><h3 class=rig-h>To scale, from above and the front</h3><div class=v da